                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> This is my config file. What should be at the place circled?\r\n\r\nNothing for most cases. The default `require('mini.completion').setup()` should be enough to show completion from LSP servers.\r\n\r\nIf LSP server tends to supply snippets which are not labeled as \"Snippet\" kind, you might want to disable this capability until #886 is resolved. See [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1277#issuecomment-2468268529) for more details.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is my config file. What should be at the place circled?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Nothing for most cases. The default <code class=\"notranslate\">require('mini.completion').setup()</code> should be enough to show completion from LSP servers.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If LSP server tends to supply snippets which are not labeled as \"Snippet\" kind, you might want to disable this capability until <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2302854262\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/886\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/886/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/886\">#886</a> is resolved. See <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1277#issuecomment-2468268529\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1277/hovercard\">this comment</a> for more details.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "This is my config file. What should be at the place circled?\n\nNothing for most cases. The default require('mini.completion').setup() should be enough to show completion from LSP servers.\nIf LSP server tends to supply snippets which are not labeled as \"Snippet\" kind, you might want to disable this capability until #886 is resolved. See this comment for more details.",
